              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घूमणो — ghūmṇo — \"to stroll; to go round\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आथण हूं बाजार मांय घूमूं हूं। āthaṇ hū̃ bājār mā̃y ghūmū̃ hū̃. In the evening I stroll round the market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): हूं सहर मांय घूम्यो, hū̃ sahar mā̃y ghūmyo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घूमणो (ghūmṇo) is inherited from a reconstructed ghummati, \"revolves\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry, but lists Hindi ghūmnā, \"to revolve, wander\" (CDIAL 4485)."
            }
          ]
        },
